    // than 100 attention sessions): PostgreSQL 17 3.56 ms → 0.19 ms and MySQL 8.0.46 9.62 ms →
    // 0.099 ms at 0.5% attention; 3.21 → 0.40 ms and 10.3 → 0.24 ms at 2%. The win shrinks as
    // selectivity rises (at 42% PostgreSQL 0.60 → 0.44 ms) because a dense attention set lets the
    // baseline plan hit the limit early too.
    //
